<title>GERMANY: Helaba H1 oper profit down 2.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Helaba H1 oper profit down 2.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    154.6  vs 159.1</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 525.1  vs 447.2</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     51.4   vs 61.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the publicly-owned German regional bank is Landesbank Hessen-Thueringen Girozentrale. Results compare with six twelfths of the full-year 1995.  </p>
<p>    Group own-account trade loss	   22.5   vs 48.9 profit</p>
<p>    Group administration costs	     393    vs 395.4</p>
<p>    Group risk provisions		    22.2   vs 28.4</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total	    166,900  vs 157,200</p>
<p>    Group lending volume		   119,800  vs 114,800</p>
<p>    Group business volume		  182,900  vs 171,700</p>
<p>NOTE - Balance sheet total, lending, business volume compare with end-1995.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
